# AC-2 — Presigned upload

Covered by `MediaIT#shouldUploadProcessPublishExposeAndThenHideMedia` (real PostgreSQL + MinIO):

- `POST /admin-api/media/uploads` creates `UPLOADED` media and returns a presigned PUT for `private/<uuid>/original`.
- Presigned request signs bucket/key/content-type/content-length; a body with a different length is rejected by MinIO.
- Browser/HttpClient uploads directly to MinIO; file bytes do not pass through admin-api/hotel-api.
- `complete` performs HEAD + magic-byte + size/dimension validation.
- `expiresAt` is approximately now + 10 minutes.
- Original object is private; anonymous GET -> 403; signed GET (admin preview) -> 200.
- Published variants are copied to `public/*`; anonymous GET -> 200 `image/webp`; anonymous PUT/list -> 403.
- `MediaUploadServiceTest` covers start validation before presigning.

Result: PASS (MediaIT 7/7, MediaUploadServiceTest).
